# The settings players toggle, each both ways, with autolist before and after: the auto commands, autoall, brief,
# compact, show, combine, noloot, nofollow, nosummon and telnetga. Then scroll and wimpy with each of their checks.
# Weary is a level-2 warrior (29 hit points at most) in the temple.
@connect weary
Weary
psswrd
@return
autolist
autoassist
autoexit
autogold
autoloot
autosac
autosplit
autolist
autoassist
autoexit
autogold
autoloot
autosac
autosplit
# autoall takes "on" or "off" exactly (strcmp): case and extra words matter.
autoall on
autolist
autoall off
autoall ON
autoall on now
autoall
brief
look
brief
compact
compact
show
score
show
combine
combine
noloot
autolist
noloot
nofollow
nosummon
telnetga
autolist
nofollow
nosummon
telnetga
@state
# scroll: what it is, paging off, the bounds, then a number past an int (atoi keeps its low 32 bits: 4294967306 is
# 10) and one past a long (clamped to LONG_MAX, whose low 32 bits are -1).
scroll
scroll foo
scroll 0
scroll
scroll 9
scroll 101
scroll 10
scroll 100
scroll 4294967306
scroll 99999999999999999999
scroll
scroll 24
# wimpy: a fifth of the most hit points by default, never more than half, never below 0.
wimpy
wimpy -1
wimpy 15
wimpy 14
wimpy 0
wimpy foo
score
